# The build context of a worker image is the repository root (workers/files/Dockerfile: `docker build -f workers/files/Dockerfile .`; workers/heartbeat/Dockerfile likewise), so this
# keeps it to what the image copies and nothing else: the repository's other files (the application, the tests, the docs, node_modules, .env files,
# .git) never reach the daemon and can never end up in an image. A new worker adds what it copies here, on purpose.
*
!package.json
!package-lock.json
!lib/service-signing.ts
!lib/canonical-json.ts
!workers/files
!workers/heartbeat
**/node_modules
